  "documentation": {
	"summary": "Wave propagation: a neighbour responds",
	"layout": "24x40 m gallery. Separate foreground lattice and sculpture; rear moving wave tiles recessed into a 13x19 m open basin. Three-metre full-width ramps connect the museum deck to a quiet rim one metre below it. Outer side aisles remain. A four-metre extension provides a level exit landing beyond the climb.",
	"objective": "Compare local neighbour coupling with a prescribed radial display. Reconstruct the relationship with a small row of the carried PointBody spheres.",
	"key_elements": [
	  "Five earlier authored artifacts retained. No curriculum reordering.",
	  "Lattice at (6,10); panel reached from the east. Bonds reveal adjacent relations; independent mode hides them.",
	  "Student bay hall-local (12,0,11), yaw180, scale1. The lesson creates its own row, rods and readout.",
	  "Wave pool x6..19 z16..35, bottom -2.2m; wave tile rim -1m, with ramps at both ends. No glass lid or fire. Interior wave rule retained, amplitude eases to zero at the access rim.",
      "Dark sphere moved to dry side aisle (21,32). All five exhibits retained."
	]
  },
